{"type":"message","id":"85a20713","parentId":"6aecad56","timestamp":"2026-10-17T22:50:52.662Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `parse_date` in `dates/parse.py`: it now uses `datetime.fromisoformat(s)` instead of `strptime`, so timestamps ending in `Z` parse. All 3 tests in `tests/test_parse.py` now pass, including `test_dates`.\n\n- **What you get back:** a timestamp ending in `Z` now gives a timezone-aware UTC datetime (`tzinfo=timezone.utc`). A timestamp with no timezone still gives a plain datetime with no timezone, as before.\n- **Python version:** this needs Python 3.11 or newer. Older versions of `fromisoformat` reject `Z`. The repo doesn't state a minimum version; it was tested on 3.13.5.\n- **Wider input:** it also accepts other ISO-8601 forms the old format rejected, such as `+02:00` offsets and fractional seconds.\n- **Possible snag:** code that compares or subtracts a UTC result against a timestamp with no timezone will raise `TypeError`. `day_key` is unaffected."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"vertex-anthropic","model":"claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":351,"cacheRead":25496,"cacheWrite":1628,"totalTokens":27477,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cttl":{"ephemeral5m":1628}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1792277448848,"responseId":"msg_vrtx_011Cg8dMiAd98N7xxyuV75ip","duration":3804.7330379999985,"ttft":3787.556407,"contextSnapshot":{"promptTokens":27126,"nonMessageTokens":21589,"compactionEpoch":0}}}
